ly"}, "tenant_proposal_required": {"description": "tenant-bearing authority state requires a tenant-aware proposal", "reason_kind": "typed_only"}, "undeclared_payload_field": {"description": "undeclared payload field", "reason_kind": "typed_only"}, "unknown_action": {"description": "unknown action", "reason_kind": "typed_only"}, "unsupported_manifest_version": {"description": "unsupported manifest version", "reason_kind": "typed_only"}}, "count": 172, "sha256_of_codes_in_order": "317bcd0957ad479c0e0b5fe49dbb886186e5180292e4942ce01f01470c5cab86"}}, "runtime_authority_string_constants": [",", "58b29ef74b9bd49d3eae7278d8cce73c7cbc6a1095a07f7b9fa44f48a7b8c07f", "An attributable lifecycle observation supplied by the trusted adapter.", "Authenticate producer bytes and evaluate only the declared criterion.", "Bind governed inputs, criteria, catalogue and purpose to actual approval.", "Bounded typed predicates; never evaluates source-supplied code.", "Describe reconsideration prerequisites; never permission to dispatch.", "Detach trusted configuration from caller-owned mutable dictionaries.", "Host-governed action classification, outside the grant write path.", "Opt-in runtime-authority/0.1 contracts. No production trust is implied.", "Opt-in terminal-revocation/0.1: revocation is terminal for a grant revision.\n\n    With it, a grant whose retained resolution checks already observed ``revoked`` for the same ``(grant_id, revision)`` is\n    refused (``grant_revocation_recorded``) at decision and at effect time, even when the status read now says ``active``. A\n    new grant revision is the way back. ``suspended`` stays reversible. The memory is this control plane's own record store:\n    a revocation it never observed cannot be remembered, and the store has no keyed integrity check.\n    ", "The pinned sha256 of the registry file a label names. Fails closed (``ValueError``) on any unsupported or non-string label:\n    there is no fallback meaning for an unknown label.", "The registry label a row's reasons need: 0.1 unless a code only 0.2 registers is present (then 0.2, a superset of 0.1), and 0.3\n    (a superset of 0.2) only when one of the eight policy-binding codes is present.\n\n    Rows that carry no opt-in-profile code keep the pinned 0.1 label and every existing 0.2 row keeps 0.2, so nothing is reinterpreted.", "True only when ``label`` is supported, every reason is listed in ``registry_codes`` (the consumer's loaded registry for that label:\n    existence is established only against it, never by this function alone) and no code is under a label that predates it. A 0.3 code\n    under 0.1 or 0.2, a 0.2 code under 0.1, an unsupported label and any unlisted code are refused.", "Trusted host configuration. Public keys are never selected by evidence.", "Validate approval-owned prerequisites using the reads used by the gate.\n\n    ``purpose_cache`` (reversibility/0.1 only) is called when the purpose status is unreadable: ``(purpose, ref, action_class) ->\n    (accepted PurposeStatus or None, reason codes, observed extras)``. Without it a purpose outage refuses for every class.", "action_blocked", "after", "age_bound_seconds", "age_extension_authority_unconfigured", "age_extension_exceeds_limit", "age_extension_invalid", "age_extension_irreversible_class", "age_extension_self_signed", "age_extension_signer_not_configured", "age_extension_unsigned", "approval", "approval_commitment", "approval_commitment_version", "approval_commitment_version_unsupported", "approval_policy_activation_mismatch", "approval_policy_generation_invalid", "approval_policy_generation_mismatch", "approval_policy_generation_missing", "attempt_unresolved_past_horizon", "authoritative", "authority_domain", "authority_limit_malformed", "authorization", "before", "bounded_tolerance", "c7678fa766f4d67d71ad9533672afdc87b3765ac1d336acae26504fc74ce3be6", "catalogue_digest", "check_expired_before_dispatch", "check_lease_unavailable", "check_overdue", "closed", "commitm